From 7084f70083e142bdf56cafc39a1e987c824343be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:18:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: a locked Settings cell says why on hover

Every lock the Settings page applies now names its cause in the cell's
title, so hovering a greyed control explains it: MLO holds the scheduler,
the mode lacks 802.11ax, Legacy mode, WMM off, AMPDU RTS off, MU-MIMO
forces beamforming, pre-emptive Bluetooth coexistence forces bursting off,
the channel or bandwidth rows need a fixed channel or an Auto width, Disable
802.11b sets the preamble, a fixed channel parks the auto-channel options.
setHardLock() takes the reason as a fourth argument and removes the title
when the lock lifts; the paired preamble lock and the auto-channel cell do
the same. No visible text: greyed stays the signal, the reason is the hover.

RWFP_67-82 in all 25 packs (RWFP_49 reused for the auto-channel cell),
lockstep 7035.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
